# Hydrazoic_acid was added on 10/1/2026. Like Internal_phosphate_polyphos_chain
# and Initial_phosphate_like_in_ATP_ADP, it was not determined from the
# training data. The neutralizer adds a proton to the terminal N- of HN3,
# giving H-N=[N+]=N-H, which Azide also matches. Azide removes only one proton
# and claims the other nitrogen as context, so the azide anion was never
# produced. This entry claims both protons first. The first (match index 1)
# exists in water only as an artifact of neutralization, so it uses the same
# always-deprotonated convention as Nitro. The second (match index 3) is the
# HN3 N-H, for which the Azide mean and standard deviation are reused; they
# match the aqueous value:
#   hydrazoic acid 4.65 (25 C, I=0): quoted in Betterton EA, Robinson JL
#     (1997) J Air Waste Manage Assoc, doi:10.1080/10473289.1997.10464060
#     (compiled value; primary source not yet verified)
*Hydrazoic_acid	[H]-[N+0:1]=[N+:2]=[N+0:3]-[H]	1	-1000.0	0	3	4.65	0.07071067811865513

*Azide	[N+0:1]=[N+:2]=[N+0:3]-[H]	2	4.65	0.07071067811865513
Nitro	[C,c,N,n,O,o:1]-[NX3:2](=[O:3])-[O:4]-[H]	3	-1000.0	0
AmidineGuanidine1	[N:1]-[C:2](-[N:3])=[NX2:4]-[H:5]	3	12.025333333333334	1.5941046150769165

