# Carboxamide was added on 10/1/2026 and was not determined from the training
# data. Amide was fit to a set that mixes activated amides (pKa as low as 3.4)
# with ordinary ones (13 to 19), so its window reached physiological pH, and
# simple amides, anilides, lactams, and peptide backbone N-H were
# deprotonated. This entry covers only amides whose carbonyl carbon and
# nitrogen bear no substituent other than carbon or hydrogen. Ureas,
# carbamates, and hydrazides still fall through to Amide. The mean is the only
# aqueous N-H pKa of a simple carboxamide in the IUPAC Digitized pKa Dataset
# (doi:10.5281/zenodo.7236452):
#   acetamide 15.1 (25 C): Branch GEK, Clayton JO (1928) J Am Chem Soc
#     50:1680, doi:10.1021/ja01393a023
# A single value has no spread, so the standard deviation of 1.0 follows
# Internal_phosphate_polyphos_chain. At the default precision the window
# starts at pH 14.1.
*Carboxamide	[CX3;!$(C(=O)(-[#7])-[!#6;!#1]):1](=[O:2])-[NX3+0;!$(N(-C=O)-[!#6;!#1]):3]-[H]	2	15.1	1.0

*Amide	[C:1](=[O:2])-[N:3]-[H]	2	12.00611111111111	4.512491341218857
*Sulfonamide	[SX4:1](=[O:2])(=[O:3])-[NX3+0:4]-[H]	3	7.9160326086956525	1.9842121316708763
Anilines_primary	[c:1]-[NX3+0:2]([H:3])[H:4]	1	3.899298673194805	2.068768503987161

# [!#1] tests for a non-hydrogen atom. The earlier [!H] tested for an H count
# other than one, so N-CH(R)R' substituents fell through to the amine group.
# Delocalized nitrogens are excluded for the same reason as in the amine group
# (below).
Anilines_secondary	[c:1]-[NX3+0;!$(N-C=[O,S,N]);!$(N-S(=O)=O);!$(N-N=[O,C]);!$(N-C#N):2]([H:3])[!#1:4]	1	4.335408163265306	2.1768842022330843
Anilines_tertiary	[c:1]-[NX3+0;!$(N-C=[O,S,N]);!$(N-S(=O)=O);!$(N-N=[O,C]);!$(N-C#N):2]([!#1:3])[!#1:4]	1	4.16690685045614	2.005865735782679

# Diazine was added on 10/1/2026 and was not determined from the training
# data. It covers pyridine-type nitrogens that share a six-membered aromatic
# ring with a second such nitrogen (pyrimidines, pyrazines, pyridazines, and
# their benzo-fused analogs). These are two to five pKa units weaker bases
# than pyridine, but the Aromatic_nitrogen_unprotonated window reaches 6.43.
# Because each ring nitrogen is a separate site, that rule also produced
# dications, whose second pKa is near -6. Rings bearing any exocyclic
# substituent other than carbon, hydrogen, or halogen (e.g., amino, oxo,
# alkoxy) are excluded and keep the generic rule, because donors raise the
# pKa sharply (trimethoprim is ~7). As with Azole_NH, one aqueous pKaH per
# parent heterocycle was taken from the IUPAC Digitized pKa Dataset
# (doi:10.5281/zenodo.7236452):
#   pyrimidine 1.23 and pyridazine 2.24 (20 C): Albert A, Goldacre R,
#     Phillips J (1948) J Chem Soc 2240
#   pyrazine 0.65 (27 C): Chia AS, Trimble RF (1961) J Phys Chem 65:863
#   cinnoline 2.27 (20 C): Osborn AR, Schofield K, Short LN (1956) J Chem
#     Soc 4191
#   phthalazine 3.47 (20 C): Albert A, Armarego WLF, Spinner E (1961) J Chem
#     Soc 2689
#   quinazoline 1.95 (20 C): Bunting JW, Perrin DD (1967) J Chem Soc B 950.
#     This is the pK of the anhydrous cation. The equilibrium value (3.4)
#     includes covalent hydration of the cation, which is not modeled here.
#   quinoxaline 0.56 (20 C): Albert A, Phillips JN (1956) J Chem Soc 1294
Diazine	[n+0;X2;$(n1:[nX2]:a:a:a:a1),$(n1:a:[nX2]:a:a:a1),$(n1:a:a:[nX2]:a:a1);!$(n1:a(!@[!#6;!#1;!F;!Cl;!Br;!I]):a:a:a:a1);!$(n1:a:a(!@[!#6;!#1;!F;!Cl;!Br;!I]):a:a:a1);!$(n1:a:a:a(!@[!#6;!#1;!F;!Cl;!Br;!I]):a:a1):1]	0	1.7671428571428571	1.0330652494028678

# Tetrazole ring nitrogens are excluded. They are roughly nine pKa units less
# basic than the pyridine-type nitrogens this group was fit to, so matching
# them produced tetrazolium variants at physiological pH.
Aromatic_nitrogen_unprotonated	[n+0&H0;!$(n1nnnc1);!$(n1nncn1):1]	0	4.3535441240733945	2.0714072661859584

# Nitrogens whose lone pair is delocalized into an adjacent C=O, C=S, C=N,
# S(=O)=O, N=O, N=C, or C#N are excluded. They are not basic in water, and
# matching them protonated, e.g., tertiary amides, thioureas, and nitrosamines.
Amines_primary_secondary_tertiary	[C:1]-[NX3+0;!$(N-C=[O,S,N]);!$(N-S(=O)=O);!$(N-N=[O,C]);!$(N-C#N):2]	1	8.159107682388349	2.5183597445318147

# e.g., [*]P(=O)(O[H])[*]. Note that cannot match the internal phosphates of ATP, because
# oxygen is not among [C,c,N,n,F,Cl,Br,I]
Phosphinic_acid	[PX4:1](=[O:2])(-[C,c,N,n,F,Cl,Br,I:3])(-[C,c,N,n,F,Cl,Br,I:4])-[OX2:5]-[H]	4	2.9745	0.6867886750744557

# e.g., [*]OP(=O)(O[H])O[*]. Cannot match ATP because P not among [C,c,N,n,F,Cl,Br,I]
Phosphate_diester	[PX4:1](=[O:2])(-[OX2:3]-[C,c,N,n,F,Cl,Br,I:4])(-[O+0:5]-[C,c,N,n,F,Cl,Br,I:4])-[OX2:6]-[H]	6	2.7280434782608696	2.5437448856908316

# e.g., [*]P(=O)(O[H])O[*]. Cannot match ATP because O not among [C,c,N,n,F,Cl,Br,I].
Phosphonate_ester	[PX4:1](=[O:2])(-[OX2:3]-[C,c,N,n,F,Cl,Br,I:4])(-[C,c,N,n,F,Cl,Br,I:5])-[OX2:6]-[H]	5	2.0868	0.4503028610465036

Primary_hydroxyl_amine	[C,c:1]-[O:2]-[NH2:3]	2	4.035714285714286	0.8463816543155368
*Indole_pyrrole	[c;R:1]1[c;R:2][c;R:3][c;R:4][n;R:5]1[H]	4	14.52875	4.06702491591416

# Azole_NH was added on 10/1/2026. Like Internal_phosphate_polyphos_chain and
# Initial_phosphate_like_in_ATP_ADP, it was not determined from the training
# data. Without it, the N-H of imidazoles, pyrazoles, triazoles, benzimidazoles,
# and purines falls through to Aromatic_nitrogen_protonated (pKa 7.17), so these
# rings were deprotonated at physiological pH. The mean and standard deviation
# are computed from one experimental aqueous N-H pKa per parent heterocycle, so
# the standard deviation reflects the spread between ring types rather than
# experimental scatter within a class. Sources were traced through the IUPAC
# Digitized pKa Dataset (doi:10.5281/zenodo.7236452):
#   imidazole 14.52 (25 C): Walba H, Isensee RW (1956) J Org Chem 21:702
#   benzimidazole 12.78 (25 C): Walba H, Isensee RW (1961) J Org Chem
#     26:2789-2791, doi:10.1021/jo01066a039
#   pyrazole 14.21 (25 C): Yagil G (1967) Tetrahedron 23:2855-2861,
#     doi:10.1016/0040-4020(67)85151-2 (aqueous KOH, H_ acidity scale)
#   1,2,4-triazole 10.26 (20 C): Kroger CF, Freiberg W (1965) Z Chem 5:381
#   1,2,3-triazole 9.4: Albert A (1963) Physical Methods in Heterocyclic
#     Chemistry, Vol. 1, p. 98 (compiled value; primary source not yet verified)
# Tetrazoles (N-H pKa ~4.9) are deliberately excluded and still match
# Aromatic_nitrogen_protonated. Rings bearing an exocyclic C=O or C=S (e.g.,
# 1,2,4-oxadiazol-5-ones) are also excluded, because they are far more acidic.
*Azole_NH	[n;$(n1naaa1),$(n1anaa1);!$(n1nnnc1);!$(n1nncn1);!$(n1c(=[O,S])aaa1);!$(n1ac(=[O,S])aa1):1]-[H]	0	12.234	2.3106665704943237
*Aromatic_nitrogen_protonated	[n:1]-[H]	0	7.17	2.94602395490212
